      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•Prestigious Upper Cliff Road location, just off Thormanby Road and moments from Howth Village and Harbour.\r\n\r\n•Situated within the protected Howth Special Amenity Area, encompassing approximately 550 hectares of outstanding natural beauty.\r\n\r\n•Charming extended two-bedroom cottage extending to approx. 80 sq.m. (861 sq.ft.).\r\n\r\n•Generous private site with substantial rear garden.\r\n\r\n•Potential for further development, subject to planning permission.\r\n\r\n•External utility room, garden shed, and greenhouse.\r\n\r\n•Beautifully private gardens with mature planting.\r\n\r\n•Walking distance to Howth Harbour, village amenities, cafés, restaurants, and shops.\r\n\r\n•Immediate access to the renowned East Cliff Walk and coastal walking trails.\r\n\r\n•Close to Deer Park, Howth Castle grounds, and Balscadden Beach.\r\n\r\n•Excellent transport links including nearby bus services and Howth DART Station.\r\n\r\n•Dublin City Centre accessible in approximately 30 minutes.\r\n\r\n•Rare opportunity to acquire a unique coastal property in one of Dublin's most sought-after seaside locations."
